"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[22398],{22398:function(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"content":"\\n<center>\\n<BookCard \\n          cover=\\"/assets/snippets/books/the-boy-who-plays-the-rainbow.png\\"\\n          title=\\"The Boy Who Plays the Rainbow\\"\\n          author=\\"Keigo Higashino\\"\\n          publisher=\\"Jaein\\"\\n          publishedDate=\\"2014-09-16\\"\\n          isbn=\\"9788990982568\\"\\n          rating=3\\n          tags=\\"thriller\\"\\n        />\\n</center>\\n\\n## Review\\nI liked the fresh subject matter of <mark>light performance</mark>, that is, <mark>Light Music</mark>, which embeds and radiates messages in light.  \\nIn particular, the term <mark>Light Music</mark> itself was fresh.  \\n<br>\\nHowever, the story itself was not fresh.  \\nSomewhat common conspiracies and interference from the powerful, and the protagonist and surrounding characters who stand up against them.  \\nIt also includes a cringey Japanese-style emotional ending, making it feel like watching a Japanese school-themed manga.  \\n<br>\\nI think it will be remembered as a work with only a good ```subject matter```.\\n"}')}}]);